**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The kit's app cache gains the Planner's folder, reached through two proxy verbs (001 §M 'Cache: … stored in the kit's `.oc/planner/` (derived, safe to delete, never sent)'; 001 §A '.oc/ app-owned cache and lock; safe to delete'; .spec-md §3.12 'A read-only open writes nothing: no .oc/lock, no .oc/planner/'; .spec-md §5 `KitProxy`: 'Fields grow as kinds land'). Sending already leaves `.oc/` out (`KitFile.sendChoiceOf`, step 196, whose facts place `.oc/planner/c.json`, step 198), so 'never sent' holds with no change here. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S14.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`: `KitRelativePath` (step 123) gains `static member plannerCacheFolder : KitRelativePath`, `appCacheFolder` (step 196) followed by `/planner`, so the text `.oc` stays written once. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs`: `KitProxy` (step 125) gains two fields, each with a one-line doc: `readPlannerCacheFile : FileName -> Result<KitFileText option, KitError>`, the text of `<plannerCacheFolder>/<name>` or `None` when there is none; and `writePlannerCacheFile : FileName -> KitFileText -> Result<unit, KitError>`, which creates or replaces that file whole, creating `.oc` and `.oc/planner` when missing as the lock creates `.oc` (step 129). A name holding `/` or `\\`, `.` or `..`, or no character answers `InvalidKitPathErr` and touches nothing, so neither verb reaches outside the planner folder. `KitProxy.readOnlyView` (step 131) refuses `writePlannerCacheFile` with `KitReadOnlyErr` naming it and passes `readPlannerCacheFile` through. (3) `KitProxy.createInMemory` keeps the texts in the folder's one map under their kit-relative paths, which `paths` lists with `.oc` and `.oc/planner`. (4) `KitProxy.create` (`OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitFolderStore.fs`, step 126) reads with a leading byte-order mark dropped and writes through `writeBytesAtomically` (step 126) as UTF-8 without one; IO exceptions are `KitIoErr` as there. No delete, listing or eviction verb is added: the cache is safe to delete by hand, and an entry nothing asks for is never read. Tests, each in `KitProxyTests` (the in-memory folder) and `KitProxyFolderTests` (a folder under the test output), over an initialised kit: `a planner cache file is written under .oc/planner and read back, and a name reaching outside it is refused`: `readPlannerCacheFile` of `a.candidate-json` answers `None`; after `writePlannerCacheFile` of it with `{}` the kit holds `.oc/planner/a.candidate-json` (`paths`, or the file on disk) and the read answers `Some` of `{}`; a second write replaces it; the names `../x.candidate-json` and `p/x.candidate-json` answer `InvalidKitPathErr` and nothing is written. `a read-only kit refuses a planner cache write and still reads the cache`: through `readOnlyView` a write answers `KitReadOnlyErr` and the kit is unchanged, and a file the read-write proxy wrote is read back.

**Acceptance.** After the verbs land, `KitProxy.readPlannerCacheFile` and `writePlannerCacheFile` MUST read and write files only directly under `.oc/planner/` in both stores, the read-only view refusing the write and passing the read; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a planner cache file is written under .oc/planner and read back, and a name reaching outside it is refused` and `a read-only kit refuses a planner cache write and still reads the cache` in both `KitProxyTests` and `KitProxyFolderTests`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s46 invariants MUST pass.
